पैतामह पैतामह, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. पिता-
मह), belonging or relating to a paternal grand-
father; derived or inherited from a grandfather;
belonging or relating to Brahmā, derived from
Brahmā, governed or presided over by Brahmā;
(अस्), m. a son of Brahmā, a patronymic of Manu;
(आस्), m. pl. forefathers, ancestors.
—पैतामह-
तीर्थ, अम्, n., N. of a sacred bathing-place.
